  "title": "Mojave groundwater bank: a decades-old water project finds new federal momentum",
  "summary": "A funding agreement signed this week between Cadiz, Inc. and the US Bureau of Reclamation has put fresh attention on one of the American Southwest’s most contested water infrastructure proposals: the Mojave Groundwater Bank, a conjunctive-use groundwater storage project in southeastern California that has been seeking regulatory approval for nearly three decades. Under the agreement, […]",
